            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myogenic prosopalgia is one of the forms virtually unfamiliar to practitioners. In a majority of cases it belongs to the category of pain-related myofascial dysfunctions present in about 10% of patients with facial pains. This work deals with etiology, pathogenesis, clinical features, diagnosis and treatment of the disorder.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
